Everything under this directory comes from the GeoNames data dump
(https://download.geonames.org/export/dump/), made by GeoNames
(https://www.geonames.org/). The dump's readme.txt says:

  This work is licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 License,
  see https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
  The Data is provided "as is" without warranty or any representation of
  accuracy, timeliness or completeness.

and GeoNames' terms ask: "You should give credit to GeoNames when using data
or web services with a link or another reference to GeoNames."

Credit: GeoNames (https://www.geonames.org/), CC BY 4.0

The files under raw/<snapshot>/ are GeoNames' own, byte for byte; each
snapshot's MANIFEST.json records the URL, size, sha256 and Last-Modified of
every file.

The Parquet under parquet/<snapshot>/ was made from them:

  - the columns were named after readme.txt in snake case and typed: ids,
    population, elevation and dem as integers, latitude and longitude as
    floats, modification_date as a date, the rest as the text of the file
  - the four is_* columns of the alternate names ('1' or empty) became
    booleans
  - the gazetteer gained a point geometry from longitude and latitude
    (WGS 84) and was cut, between countries, into several files
  - rows were sorted; values were not changed otherwise

The code that fetches, checks and converts is MIT, in the repository this
dataset was built from (https://github.com/yuiseki/geonames), and does not
apply here.
